stream
BT /F1 18 Tf 50 790 Td (Energy-Aware Adaptive Self-Speculative Decoding) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 50 762 Td (Project summary for understanding and presentation) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 50 728 Td (Motivation:) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 70 710 Td (- Reduce energy use and latency for small language models on laptops and consumer GPUs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 70 692 Td (- Keep output quality stable while avoiding wasted speculative work.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 50 658 Td (Research idea:) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 70 640 Td (- Use early-layer draft generation and full-model verification.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 70 622 Td (- Choose between ordinary decoding and speculative decoding based on energy cost.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 70 604 Td (- Use recent acceptance history and context length to decide whether a draft is worth it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 50 570 Td (Main research question:) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 70 552 Td (- When does speculative decoding actually save energy per committed token?) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 70 534 Td (- When is ordinary decoding safer and cheaper?) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 50 500 Td (Current prototype status:) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 70 482 Td (- The repo contains a synthetic controller prototype that chooses draft depth and draft length.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 70 464 Td (- It simulates energy, latency, and acceptance behavior.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 70 446 Td (- The prototype passes tests and demonstrates the controller logic.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 70 428 Td (- The real model version is prepared as the next step.) Tj ET
endstream
