7 0 obj
<< /Length 1823 >>
stream
BT /F1 18 Tf 50 790 Td (What the project does and how it works) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 50 762 Td (1. Offline preparation) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 70 744 Td (- Profile action candidates such as ordinary decoding, draft depth 4, and draft length 2 or 5.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 70 726 Td (- Measure acceptance rate, energy, latency, and memory for each configuration.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 70 708 Td (- Use calibration prompts to fit the controller policy.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 50 674 Td (2. Online inference) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 70 656 Td (- At each generation step, the controller checks the current context and acceptance history.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 70 638 Td (- It compares estimated energy per committed token against ordinary decoding.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 70 620 Td (- If expected gains are uncertain, it falls back to ordinary decoding.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 50 586 Td (3. Hardware support) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 70 568 Td (- The project is designed for CPU, CUDA, Apple MPS, Intel XPU, and simulation mode.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 70 550 Td (- An RTX 3050 setup script is included for NVIDIA users.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 70 532 Td (- Real model execution requires PyTorch, Transformers, and CUDA-enabled tooling.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 50 498 Td (4. Output and interpretation) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 70 480 Td (- Energy per token, latency, throughput, acceptance rate, action trace, and output matching are reported.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 70 462 Td (- A good result is lower energy per committed token without changing ordinary output behavior.) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 50 428 Td (Summary:) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 50 410 Td (This project is a focused research prototype for an energy-aware speculative decoding controller,) Tj ET
BT /F1 12 Tf 50 392 Td (starting from a working synthetic simulator and moving toward a real GPU-enabled evaluation pipeline.) Tj ET
endstream
